  },
  "notes": "`start_puts` is a `void` routine cast into pthread_create's `void *(*)(void *)` slot ending in a tail-called `puts`, which sets only the low four of the eight bytes returned; `warn_count`, cast into glob's `int` errfunc slot, never writes the return register. Parking either invents the return from the register's leftover (`CONCAT44(dat_4,puts(a0))`, an unset `v1`).",
  "probe_id": "p-8ee15a584aa7"
}
